==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from [[w:Warehouse (nightclub)|The Warehouse]], a [[nightclub]] in [[Chicago]], [[Illinois]], USA, where the music became popular around 1985.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhaʊs ˌmjuːzɪk/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|music genre}} A particular type of [[electronic]] [[dance music]] with an [[uptempo]] beat and recurring [[kickdrum]].
#: {{syn|en|house}}
#: {{hypo|en|microhouse}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1986|title=Move Your Body|author=w:Marshall Jefferson|passage=Gotta have '''house music''', all night long / With that '''house music''', you can't go wrong / Give me that '''house music''', set me free}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=Chuck Roberts|artist=Rhythm Controll|title=My House|year=1987|passage=House is an uncontrollable desire to jack your body / And, as I told you before, this is our house and our '''house music'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Danny Palmerlee|title=South America on a Shoestring|page=66|passage=Corrugated-steel ceilings, a dozen blue-felted pool tables and DJ '''house music''' Thursday to Saturday.}}

